---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const updated = 'July 21, 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions — AppsAnalyzer"
  description="The terms and conditions governing your use of the AppsAnalyzer Android application."
>
  <article class="legal container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of the <strong>AppsAnalyzer</strong>
      Android application ("the app"). By downloading, installing, or using the app, you agree
      to these Terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the app.
    </p>

    <h2>1. License</h2>
    <p>
      AppsAnalyzer is free and open-source software distributed under the MIT License. You are
      granted a non-exclusive, worldwide license to use, copy, modify, and distribute the app in
      accordance with that license.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided to help you analyze the technology behind applications installed on your
      own device. You agree to use it lawfully and not to misuse the app or attempt to use it to
      infringe the rights of any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Analysis Accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      AppsAnalyzer uses heuristics and a scoring system to detect frameworks such as Flutter,
      React Native, Expo, Kotlin Multiplatform, and Native Android. While we strive for accuracy,
      results are provided for informational purposes only and may occasionally misclassify an
      application. Detections should not be relied upon as definitive.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <p>
      All app, framework, and company names referenced by the app are trademarks or registered
      trademarks of their respective owners. Their use is for identification and descriptive
      purposes only and does not imply any affiliation or endorsement.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Disclaimer of Warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties of any kind, whether
      express or implied, including but not limited to the implied warranties of merchantability,
      fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the authors and contributors shall not be liable for
      any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of data or
      profits, arising out of or related to your use of the app.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Third-Party Distribution</h2>
    <p>
      If you obtain the app through a third-party platform, that platform's terms may also apply to
      your download and installation.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to These Terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the app after changes take
      effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these Terms can be raised by opening an issue on our
      <a href="https://github.com/shubham-soni9/Apps-Analyzer" rel="noopener" target="_blank">GitHub repository</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 760px;
    padding-top: 64px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--brand);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin: 8px 0 32px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
  }
  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal p strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--brand);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
